  "id": "COMPOUND:31358 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Brusatol is implicated in the biological activity leading to the target of SNU1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Brusatol acts as a target for Raji, which in turn is targeted by Radulannin A and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, both of which ultimately target SNU1. This indicates a chain of molecular targets that may contribute to the effect of Brusatol on SNU1. The presence of multiple pathways converging on SNU1 suggests that Brusatol may influence SNU1 through different mechanisms, potentially involving various compounds that share a common target. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Brusatol and SNU1, emphasizing the importance of understanding the interplay between these molecular entities in the context of their biological roles.",
